                <pb facs="1070" n="934" sameAs="frus:frus1929v01/pg934"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">717.2114/85: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Eberhardt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-02-08T12:00:00-05:45">February 8,
                        1929—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 2:55 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>43. Department’s 23, February 2, 8 p.m. In compliance with the Department’s
                    instructions I have again discussed the matter with the <pb facs="1071" n="935"
                        xml:id="pg935"/> President and he told me that he would urge approval of the
                    treaty during the present session of Congress.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Eberhardt</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
